trigger_ci", "args": {"ref": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-bankers-rounding-08d3cd5986", "confidence": 0.94}, "confidence": 0.94}, {"t_ms": 13698, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01RRAAqmvB616KdbkKnwPdpj", "tool": "trigger_ci", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-bankers-rounding-08d3cd5986", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 13698, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01RRAAqmvB616KdbkKnwPdpj", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 15697, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01HNNTCzgerrCTm6rcmBiWrP", "tool": "wait_for_ci", "args": {"run_id": "ci-0001", "confidence": 0.95}, "confidence": 0.95}, {"t_ms": 373698, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01HNNTCzgerrCTm6rcmBiWrP", "tool": "wait_for_ci", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 373698, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01HNNTCzgerrCTm6rcmBiWrP", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 379164, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01CCHdyMSYVUdrgVotw8U9ZS", "tool": "open_pr", "args": {"head": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "## Summary\n`round_money` in `src/money.py` was documented as using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212) but actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. This caused `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` to fail in the nightly build (`2.665` rounded to `2.67` instead of `2.66`).\n\n## Change\n- Switch the rounding mode from `ROUND_HALF_UP` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, which matches the docstring and FIN-212.\n\n## Testing\n- CI run `ci-0001` passed on commit `08d3cd5986`.\n\n## Note\nThis changes how amounts that end in exactly half a cent get rounded (they now go to the nearest even cent). Please check whether any downstream consumers depended on the old round-half-up behavior.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-bankers-rounding", "confidence": 0.93}, "confidence": 0.93}, {"t_ms": 380064, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01CCHdyMSYVUdrgVotw8U9ZS", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-bankers-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 380064, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01CCHdyMSYVUdrgVotw8U9ZS", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 383881, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and the pull request is open against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `src/money.py`'s `round_money` says it uses banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212) but actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. So `2.665` rounded to `2.67` instead of the `2.66` the test expects.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-bankers-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (commit `08d3cd5986`).\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** #101 (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101).\n\nI haven't merged it, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval. One thing to watch: amounts ending in exactly half a cent will now round to the nearest even cent. I noted this in the PR in case anything downstream relied on the old behavior.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by looking at the repository and the relevant files.", "type":